  "generated_text": "1. **Identify the total number of slices**: The pizza has 12 slices.\n2. **Identify the number of slices with pepperoni**: There are 6 slices with pepperoni.\n3. **Identify the number of slices with mushrooms**: There are 10 slices with mushrooms.\n4. **Use the principle of inclusion-exclusion**: Since every slice has at least one topping, we can use the principle of inclusion-exclusion to find the number of slices with both pepperoni and mushrooms. The formula is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total slices} = \\text{Slices with pepperoni} + \\text{Slices with mushrooms} - \\text{Slices with both pepperoni and mushrooms}\n   \\]\n   Substituting the known values:\n   \\[\n   12 = 6 + 10 - \\text{Slices with both pepperoni and mushrooms}\n   \\]\n   Simplifying, we get:\n   \\[\n   12 = 16 - \\text{Slices with both pepperoni and mushrooms}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Slices with both pepperoni and mushrooms} = 16 - 12 = \\boxed{4}\n",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[4, '4']",
    "gold_answer": "There are 12 total slices, and 6 of them have pepperoni and 10 have mushrooms. Let $n$ be the number of the slices that have both toppings, so there are $6-n$ with just pepperoni and $10-n$ with just mushrooms.  Since every slice has at least one topping, and there are 12 slices, we must have $(6-n) + (10-n) + n = 12$, which gives $n=\\boxed{4}$.",
    "is_correct": true
